  "body": "## Problem\n\nThe Trochoidal method of 2D Adaptive checks the tool engagement for each lane. It does not check the clean-up passes after the lanes. A worker that studied #1587 read engagements of up to 102.5 deg on the clean-up passes, against the limit of 90 deg.\n\nThe readings came from a trial branch, but the check is also missing on main. The result is a possible silent overload of the cutter. It is not a gouge.\n\n## Why P1\n\nAGENTS.md, Prime Directive: a result that is not safe must be refused, or the toolpath must give a visible diagnostic. An engagement above the limit that passes without a note can break the cutter.\n\n## Fix\n\n- Apply the same engagement check to the clean-up passes as to the lanes.\n- A clean-up pass above the limit is cut in smaller steps, or it gets a named warning on the operation and in the status line. It never passes silently.\n- Pin: on the fixture of #1587, no clean-up move is above the limit without a named warning. The pin is red first on main.\n\n## Notes\n\n- Found during the read-only study for the recommended option on #1587.\n- Related: #1587, #3754, #3759.\n",
